    {
      "id": 15947,
      "name": "MindWanderer",
      "username": "MindWanderer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-12-16T01:05:34.000Z",
      "cooked": "<div>\n<span>Normally, incapacitated heroes can't use powers at all, even if they have one from some source other than their own cards, because the rules say that the only thing they can do during their turn is use an incapacitated ability. &nbsp;The rules don't actually say they have no \"use a power\"&nbsp;</span><em>phase</em><span>. &nbsp;So could you conceivably use, say,&nbsp;</span><span>Infection</span><span>&nbsp;and Embolden, to give an incapacitated hero a power use? &nbsp;What about Cosmic Weapon and Dynamic Syphon? &nbsp;(In fact, it seems those can even be played directly on an incapacitated hero. &nbsp;Not that this would normally be a good idea.)</span>\n</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>\n<span>And if that works,&nbsp;</span><span>I just ran across this in the clarifications:</span>\n</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>\"If Embolden is on a hero and that hero becomes incapacitated, Embolden stays there until the end of that hero’s next turn.\"</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Presumably, this is because you can't deal damage to an incapacitated hero--unless they're Huge Skyscaper. &nbsp;That could be a highly amusing workaround.</div>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:48:30.322Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 8,
      "reads": 1,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 40.2,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 15945,
      "topic_slug": "emboldened-incapacitated-huge-skyscraper",
      "display_username": "MindWanderer",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
      "flair_bg_color": "",
      "flair_color": "",
      "flair_group_id": 41,
